::  name       radiator reading
::  shape      lines - a steady-state radiative reading and its verdict (max 8)
::  invariant  every line carries a number and its unit; the verdict line names the margin
::  example    the worked case of press/date/20260907/20260907-175821_the-radiator-and-the-wire-public.html
::  readers    brush_parse.rye -> Frame -> Skate
::  nib        surface-radiator-v0
::
::  The essay's interactive field, converted to a surface this tree can draw. The html
::  ran the arithmetic in a browser; here the surface holds the READING and the physics
::  belongs to a Rye module, per active-designing/20260908-124500_the-witness-the-essay-asked-for.md.
::  Five inputs stand behind these lines: junction temperature, coolant delta, emissivity,
::  the sink the panel faces, and geometry -- with the self-view tax named as its own term.
::
::  SIMPLE, LOVABLE, COMPLETE at its own scope: it draws one real case with real numbers,
::  including the refusal, and it claims nothing more. The inputs move when the Rye witness
::  lands; a surface that presents a computed reading it cannot yet compute would be a
::  drawing of a promise.
::  Tongue: Glow · Bron · TAME · Radiant. Never JS · HTML · CSS · JSON.
::
::  at-nib:     radiator-reading
::  present:    Frame
::  max-lines:  8
::  style:
::    paper 0xFF10161C
::    ink 0xFFE8EEF2
::  lines:
::    junction 100 C, coolant 10 K below, emissivity 0.90
::    sink 250 K, one face, self-view tax 15 percent
::    panel temperature 90 C
::    shed after tax 585 W per m2
::    one face, sink 250 K 688 W per m2
::    1.71 m2 per kW
::    150 kW wants 256 m2 of panel
::    AI1 peak 1364 W per m2 over 110 m2 refuses, short by 779
::  refuse:     src/web · Wasm/Web backend · CSS rail · a { } stylesheet · JS arithmetic
